<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rutger Jan Schimmelpenninck</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1761–1825</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rutger Jan Schimmelpenninck was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> lawyer and statesman who served as ambassador to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>. In 1805 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> made him <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-pensionary">Grand Pensionary</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batavian-republic">Batavian Republic</a> with wide powers, and he introduced a national tax system and education reforms. In 1806 Napoleon replaced the republic with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-holland">Kingdom of Holland</a> under his brother Louis.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rutger-jan-schimmelpenninck.jpg" alt="Rutger Jan Schimmelpenninck" width="320" height="518" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charles Howard Hodges · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portret_van_Rutger_Jan_Schimmelpenninck_(1761-1825).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
